## Store 172 (Edinburg) — adversarial map audit

### Pass 1 — Mechanical
`./rebuild.sh 172` rerun from scratch three times (baseline + after each fix). Final: **exit 0**, `verify: []`, `coverage.sealed_floor_patches: []`, `coverage.unreachable_shelf_labels: []`, `components {n: 1, sizes: [64040]}`, `walkable_pct 24.3` (= `reachable_pct`, inside the 20–35% band), **756 tests pass**. `provenance.drift: null`; zones/seal_zones derived, exclusions/inclusions from file.

### Pass 2 — Systematic visual sweep
3×3 crops of `walkable_overlay.png` viewed individually, each compared against the printed page 2 underneath, plus paired printed/overlay zooms of Dairy, Frozen, Market band, Floral, Sushi, Produce, Bakery NW, Deli, Pharmacy, back-room vestibule, west wall and the checkout front. To catch what page-zoom hides I also enumerated **every** connected region of `free_raw & ~free` (open floor after boundary+exclusions that ends up non-green) — 21 components ≥20 cells — and classified all of them, and re-ran that enumeration after the fix.

### Pass 3 — Label probes
Rather than 10 labels, I probed **all 261 text items** on page 2 against the shipped grid (`profile.npz`, cell 2.0 pt, `m_per_cell` 0.1763). Every product label's nearest reachable floor is ≤ **0.12 m** (Cotton 0.09, Dog Food 0.07, Napkins 0.09, Diapers 0.04, Toys 0.00, Vitamins 0.09, Sodas 0.06, Coffee 0.07, Cereal 0.09, Batteries 0.06, Bakeware 0.08, Tortillas 0.07, Bread 0.03, Wine 0.05, Water 0.07, Charcoal 0.03, Pickles 0.05, Tobacco 0.11, Party 0.02). The only items >2 m are the four red department words printed inside drawn-sealed rooms (Pharmacy, Bakery, Deli, Business Center) and the vestibule "Entrance" words — all expected.

