## Inspected and cleared (not findings)

- **Drawn-sealed blocks.** Pharmacy (x 186–356, y 628–702), Deli (x 834–989, y 657–703) and Bakery (x 990–1063, y 472–703) probe as solid in the *no-boundary* grid too — they are closed rooms in the source PDF, not sealing artifacts. None contains a product label or fixture; each has green frontage (aisle-25 corridor at y≈615; Deli counter line at y≈657; Bakery sawtooth case diagonal). This is the store-24 failure mode's shape, so I checked it hardest: the guide simply draws no interior for them. `PHARMACY`/`BAKERY` far-snaps (4.55 m / 2.51 m) are consequences of this, not defects.
- **All 10 printed culled pockets classified.** Nine are checkout-lane interiors and restroom/exit-corridor crevices between checkstands (y 616–674). The tenth, `190 cells near BAKERY at (953.6, 541.0)`, is the Produce cross-aisle that inclusion #2 restores — it probes GREEN today. Note `culled_pockets` is captured *before* inclusions are restored, which is why (555.4, 659.7) still prints at 254 cells; the surviving sealed region there is now 148 cells.
- Remaining sealed slivers (≤1.4 m²): Bakery case-front strip, Floral diagonal-display crevices, produce inter-rack gap at (1012, 462), staff swinging-door mouths on the north wall, west-wall crevice at (188, 600), Greeting Cards sliver at (362, 691) — all dead crevices with green immediately adjacent; no access lost.
- **Front vestibule** (Business Center, both restroom pairs, Entrance/Exit doors) is outside the extracted boundary polygon, consistent with the two enclosed-room `must_not` points; the sales floor's own entrance approach `[455, 698]` is green.
- **Config sanity.** Both inclusions state a WHY that matches the map (Kitchen Gadgets/Appliances are shelf tags on the open grocery floor, not a service kitchen; the Produce rect stops at x=986, short of the Bakery block at x≥990 — it does not blanket a staff area). All three exclusions match the drawn back-of-house: the vestibule rect stops at x=474 and the green sales floor correctly stops at the x=423 wall as the WHY claims; the Market back band and the NE cooler/dock poly cover only doored rooms and coolers. No exclusion removes any shelf label's only frontage — the 261-label sweep confirms this.

